With Studio, the dashboard has a Coaching side (switch at the top of the sidebar). The Studio
walkthrough in Guide takes you through it in ten short chapters, doing each thing for real.

## Practise on sample clients

The first Studio chapter offers three sample clients: Niamh, who asks to join through your first
invite link; Conor, already your client, who answers check-ins and messages; and Dara, who shares only
her training. They act on their own a few seconds after you do something, and only you ever see them.

They live in **Practice view**. With it on, a striped band runs across Coaching and every page about
people (Today, Clients, Check-ins, Messages) shows only the sample clients; nothing you do there
reaches a real person. With it off, they're out of sight everywhere, including counts and the client
picker. Your programs, check-in forms, invite links and packages are the same in both. Switch it at
the bottom of the sidebar, with Turn off on the band, or from ⌘K. Adding sample clients turns it on,
and so does a walkthrough chapter you do with them.

Keep them as a sandbox to try programs and forms on. Manage them in Practice view, on Clients: Reset
to fresh puts back their starting four weeks, Remove deletes them and everything they sent, and Add
sample clients brings them back.

